  "final_message": "I restored `channel`, because `analytics-ingest` requires it on `OrderPlaced`. That reverts my earlier removal in the files and their contents. It also reverts the matching `CLAUDE.md` and `README.md` examples, and the \"reports every problem\" validation test. After the revert, `npm test` passes all 39 tests. I haven't run CI itself.\n\nThe ARCH-4 contract check isn't in this repo, so I couldn't see it or run it. Its failure message says `analytics-ingest` still requires `OrderPlaced.channel` as `web|store|marketplace`. So something downstream does read the field, even though this service no longer does.\n\nGit now shows the restored files as modified against `HEAD`. A commit made after my removal must have taken the removal into `HEAD`. This working-tree state is the fix, and it still needs committing.\n\nTo remove `channel` for real, the `analytics-ingest` owners have to drop it from their contract first. After that the removal can go back in, with `schemaVersion` bumped to 4. Say if you'd rather keep the removal and handle that with them, and I'll redo it.\n\nI tried `git checkout -- .` to revert in one step, but it was denied (no approval is available in this session), so I undid the edits by hand.",
